cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "bicyclic-kinship: kinship reasoning without a neural network"
abstract: >-
  A sound, set-valued model of relational composition that derives its rules
  from composition facts over opaque symbols instead of learning weights. On
  the CLUTRR benchmark it reaches the level of the best published systems on
  chains longer than any seen in training, and reports when a question has
  more than one answer.
